From: Yash Dayani <52958495+YashDayani@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] SystemUI: add a network speed indicator to the status bar

Shows the current download and upload speed as a small two line
indicator in the status bar, for the networks that have working
internet (Wi-Fi and mobile data). It is off by default and is turned on
from Settings > Network & internet (companion
platform_packages_apps_Settings patch) or with:

  settings put system network_traffic_enabled 1

Further settings: network_traffic_mode (0 up and down, 1 up only,
2 down only), network_traffic_units (0 bits, 1 bytes),
network_traffic_refresh_interval (seconds), network_traffic_autohide,
network_traffic_autohide_threshold (kB/s) and network_traffic_hidearrow.

The indicator view is taken from the EvoX and crDroid SystemUI
(NetworkTraffic, Apache-2.0, crDroid Android Project) and wired into
the status bar icon pipeline of this tree:

- It reads the network_traffic_* settings of the current user from
  Settings.System with a ContentObserver (and re-reads them on user
  switch), because TunerService in this tree only reads Settings.Secure
  and has no support for the "system:" prefix EvoX uses.
- It listens to the network only while it is attached and enabled.
- The status bar tints it through DarkIconDispatcher (registered by
  DarkIconManager); the quick settings header and the keyguard tint it
  through setStaticDrawableColor() of TintedIconManager.
- PhoneStatusBarPolicy adds the slot once at start up and the view
  shows or hides itself from the settings, so it needs no new
  constructor dependencies.

- The slot only counts as visible while there is a speed to show, and
  the view keeps its width when StatusIconContainer hides it, so the
  container never lays out the neighbouring icons from a stale width.

Known limitation: it is not shown when the Compose system icons flags
are enabled.
